[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Write a marketing plan for my handmade candle shop on Etsy, as a Markdown file\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[28.954, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/etsy-candle-marketing-plan.md)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[32.209, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I've written your marketing plan to `<workspace>/etsy-candle-marketing-plan.md`. I didn't know your shop's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  details, so it's a general plan with `[brackets]` where your own information goes. The targets and budget\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  figures are example numbers, not benchmarks for your shop.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The plan has 15 sections:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Foundations:** goals, brand positioning, and target customers.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Etsy listings:** SEO guidance (titles, tags, photos), product and pricing strategy, and Etsy's own tools\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (ads, discounts, reviews).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Reaching customers:** social media, an email list, packaging, and partnerships.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Planning:** a seasonal calendar, safety and trust notes, and a 90-day checklist.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Money and tracking:** an example monthly budget and the metrics to track.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  If you give me your shop name, scents, price range and current sales, I can fill in the brackets and tailor\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the targets and budget.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[36.947, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Push it further.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[75.746, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mEdited 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Edit(<workspace>/etsy-candle-marketing-plan.md)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[80.525, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I added a \"Part 2: Going Deeper\" to `<workspace>/etsy-candle-marketing-plan.md`. It has sections 16–31, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the original sections are unchanged.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Money:** a per-candle cost and profit breakdown, with break-even ad return and a note on Etsy's Offsite\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Ads fee.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Etsy listings:** a keyword research process, a title formula, a fill-in listing description template,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and a staged Etsy Ads plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Launches and content:** a week-by-week plan for launching a new scent, a weekly social content schedule\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with video ideas, and email sequences (welcome, post-purchase, win-back).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Growth:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Customer segments and where to find them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Subscription and repeat-revenue ideas.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A reviews system.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A competitor worksheet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Six A/B tests to run one at a time.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A scaling path through year 2.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Risks and routine:** a risk table, a weekly marketing routine of about 6–8 hours, and a dashboard to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  copy into a spreadsheet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The cost and fee figures in the example are rough. Etsy's fees change, so check them against your own seller\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  dashboard before relying on the break-even numbers.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You said \"push it further\" without saying how, so I read it as \"make it deeper and more actionable.\" If you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  meant something else, I can:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Tailor it to your actual scents and prices.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Write ready-to-post captions and emails.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Draft the first listing rewrites.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Cut it down to a one-page version.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
